K-Pop boy band Cortis talk about performing their new song &#8220;Motion&#8221; with collaborator Juicy J backstage at Lollapalooza 2026.

CORTIS&nbsp;

What&#8217;s good, everybody? This is CORTIS&nbsp;

Juicy J&nbsp;

and Juicy J.&nbsp;

Welcome to Billboard. Working with him kind of came up naturally. Like it&#8217;s just like it was a natural step to take.&nbsp;

I&#8217;m in the best time of my life right now.

We just did Lollapalooza. That&#8217;s crazy.&nbsp;

Tetris Kelly&nbsp; 0:20&nbsp;&nbsp;

We&#8217;re taking you to CORTIS at Lollapalooza in Billboard All Access. Rain and weather hit Chicago, but it didn&#8217;t stop the crowd from going red, red.&nbsp;

It was a weather delay. Thank you for the waiting. Of course, we love you.

Tetris Kelly&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

And fans got the live debut of &#8220;Motion:&#8221; with Juicy J.

CORTIS&nbsp;&nbsp;

Damn, it&#8217;s kind of awkward to tell tell this story in front of y&#8217;all, in front of him, but man, I&#8217;m a big fan of him really since a young kid. I was just listening, bumping 365 all the time. Listening to all those classics is kind of really put me onto a lot of South hip hop, Southern hip hop.

It&#8217;s amazing, man. These guys are super talented, man. They can sing, they can dance, they can rap. It&#8217;s an honor to work with them, man. You know, I&#8217;m blessed to still be, you know, been in this game for a long time, over 20 years, and still go to the studio and cook up with new artists and and create hits for real, man. God is great.

